= Benchmark contamination — Technical =

== Exposure channels ==
Benchmark information can enter through:

<pre>
pretraining corpus
fine-tuning corpus
synthetic derivative data
solution/explanation text
benchmark-targeted prompt search
adaptive evaluation feedback
</pre>

Each channel creates a different dependence between model development and evaluation data.

== Detection ==
Detection methods include exact overlap, near-duplicate search, n-gram methods, membership-style inference, perturbation tests, temporal controls, watermarking, and training-corpus audits.

No detector proves absence of all contamination.

== Effect size ==
The impact depends on exposure count, similarity, optimization, model scale, regularization, later training, and forgetting.

Recent controlled studies show that contamination can inflate scores, while some exposures can also be forgotten after extensive subsequent training.

